/*
 * GameShelf - the catalog data.
 *
 * DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE. It is the "database" for this project and it is
 * already finished. Your job is to display it, filter it and sort it.
 *
 * This file is loaded by a <script> tag in index.html BEFORE your app.js,
 * which is why you can just use the GAMES variable in your own code.
 *
 * Every game is an object with the same shape:
 *
 *   id         number   unique, never changes
 *   title      string
 *   year       number   year of original release
 *   developer  string
 *   genres     array of strings   1-2 per game
 *   platforms  array of strings   "PC" | "PlayStation" | "Xbox" | "Nintendo" | "Mobile"
 *   rating     number   0.0 - 10.0, one decimal, approximate critic consensus
 *   players    string   "Single-player" | "Multiplayer" | "Both"
 *   avgHours   number   roughly how long people play it
 *   coverFrom  string   hex colour, top of the cover gradient
 *   coverTo    string   hex colour, bottom of the cover gradient
 *   blurb      string   one sentence
 *
 * Note that platforms are deliberately stored as FAMILIES ("PlayStation"),
 * not exact consoles ("PS3", "PS4", "PS5"). Real catalogues normalise data
 * like this so a filter list stays short enough to actually be usable.
 */

